  "blocks": {
    "\"Did you read what it changed in the auth flow?\"": "“你读过它对认证流程作出的改动吗？”",
    "\"Read the diff before you push, vibing on auth is how secrets leak into logs.\"": "“推送前先读 diff；在认证代码上只凭感觉，秘密信息就是这样泄漏到日志里的。”",
    "\"Vibe coded it — login still works, that's all I checked.\"": "“我用氛围编程做的——登录还能用，我只检查了这一点。”",
    "A working pattern where the user accepts the agent's code without human review. The diff is treated as opaque — what matters is whether the program behaves, not what's inside. Automated review and automated checks may still run; vibe coding is silent on both.": "氛围编程是一种工作模式：用户不经过<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/human-review\">人工审查</a>，直接接受<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>生成的代码。diff 被视为不透明黑盒——重要的是程序是否按预期运行，而不是内部具体写了什么。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-review\">自动化审查</a>和<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-check\">自动化检查</a>仍然可以运行；“氛围编程”这个概念本身并不限定两者。",
    "Avoid: \"vibe coding\" as a synonym for \"low-quality AI coding\" — the term names the review stance, not the resulting code.": "<em>避免：</em>把“氛围编程”当作“低质量 AI 编码”的同义词。这个术语描述的是审查立场，而不是最终代码质量。",
    "The cost arrives later. Vibe-coded changes accumulate into a codebase nobody has read, and behaviour was the only thing checked — so anything behaviour doesn't surface, like a secret written to logs, a missing edge case, or quietly wrong data handling, ships unseen. The first time someone debugs the system is the first time anyone reads the code. With human review gone, whatever automated verification still runs — tests, types, automated review — is the only gate the code passes through.": "代价会在之后出现。氛围编程产生的改动会累积成一个无人真正读过的代码库，而此前只检查了外在行为——凡是行为层面没有暴露的问题，例如秘密信息被写入日志、遗漏边界情况，或悄然错误的数据处理，都会在无人察觉时交付。第一次有人调试系统，也可能是第一次有人真正阅读代码。没有人工审查后，仍在运行的自动化验证——测试、类型检查和自动化审查——就成了代码通过的唯一门禁。",
    "The term comes from Andrej Karpathy, who coined it in early 2025: you \"fully give in to the vibes\" and \"forget that the code even exists\" — describe what you want, accept what comes back, and judge it by running it.": "这个术语由 Andrej Karpathy 在 2025 年初提出：你“完全跟着感觉走”，甚至“忘记代码本身的存在”——描述自己想要什么，接受返回的结果，再通过运行效果进行判断。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "Vibe coding trades inspection for speed. Reading diffs is usually the slowest step in agent-driven work, so dropping it removes the main bottleneck. For code whose failures are cheap — prototypes, one-off scripts, internal tools — that's a reasonable trade. The risk scales with the code's lifespan and stakes.": "氛围编程用检查换取速度。阅读 diff 通常是智能体驱动工作中最慢的一步，省去它就移除了主要瓶颈。对于失败成本较低的代码——<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/prototyping\">原型</a>、一次性脚本和内部工具——这可能是合理权衡。风险会随着代码寿命和重要性增长。"
  },
